do super recognisers have better than average memory in any other areas of life? Well, I can answer that. We have used object memory tests and some other sort of visual processing tests, and they tend to be slightly better than controls at these other tests, suggesting that they do have superior memory for visual things in general, but actually the differences between controls and super recognises far greater when it comes to faces. And perhaps we found voices as well. We've done some recent research, finding that they tend to be slightly better at voices, which might suggest that it's something about human identification, human recognition, rather than purely face recognition.

